  "id": "retarded-depression",
  "term": "retarded depression",
  "definition": "Retarded depression, as supported here in the phrase psychomotor-retarded depression, refers to a depressive presentation characterized by slowed psychomotor functioning and a hypoarousal-dominant state. In this counselling context, it is contrasted with more agitated or hyperaroused conditions.",
